README.md
/scripts

#  Build output. gprbuild puts objects in obj/ and executables in bin/, both inside the course
#  directory because that is where a GNAT project wants them.
#
#  These two lines do NOT stop the course editor sweeping that output into course-info.yaml's
#  additional_files. That was claimed here once, on a measurement taken a minute after opening
#  the project -- too early to see it. The editor's file watcher picks up whatever appears while
#  it is running, and writes the lot on quit; since running scripts/check_course.py rebuilds
#  everything, opening the IDE and then validating is exactly the sequence that triggers it.
#
#  check_additional_files in scripts/check_course.py is the only thing that actually holds the
#  line. It refuses to run while build output is in that list, so nothing can be committed with
#  it there. These entries stay because they are correct for the course archive regardless.
/obj
/bin
